<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>We=E2=80=99re seeing a dip in oil =
prices this morning,</strong> with Brent crude down about 1% at $103 a barr=
el, after another momentary pause in US attacks on Iran.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Prices eased overnight on news that US pre=
sident Donald Trump had pledged in a Truth Social <a href=3D"https://ablink=
.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.wtfWA9uPAn8i7Lb0U_hU2i6Zz0TTpD-zLmtPgj=
tSDHWFMQFS4t5V6IgCjeSrOGU8trAIKFFNtqlVgAOFc5ICYAzCZrKNMb4SCX-FoVekeQCJMLzYY=
YOP08ibM15BP1880-duL7rKndOaovJth_EQPyqOQ2O-ho6oI0N-Q185edwCaPKvuZeXM-inrm1d=
gq6Xy4cGHBmXcokbXD1lRpwzO0dgugOv95ibd1XcM29Er0dLCFXiWbEEsy6cHwKugGLiX1rQrn7=
qF1y_wYUAwletRQ/4uq/jUICq9qARSGfk2tRSsZkkw/h30/h001.SnYVx9UP51GU2D5pVy4vnPU=
xUTBUj7PbirrONx5GWVs" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">post</a> not to attack Iran=
 ahead of the US midterm elections, which take place on 3 November.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It comes as public support for his war in =
the Middle East is waning and ultimately weighing on Republican election ca=
mpaigns.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">An <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR4TlkV015Ok9576v5vLffIxSgah70-r-=
4Dv_6d-l6-KtNbstUtemD44Esv5MXkxTuztE61gmL23yIw-ibihm3RVbW8gi8fq2PwbrzTH1cnR=
sw2rtQGTCuYFR4s-Rl5UON7iy_wI31O4MvdKJt8aTgO-ILFZN50J9J1XyCivjLm0YwkVlqJohhD=
FwlI8VsxrH7Hq-N8dlmISh3Rb0eryGGAQtfssneiW1ftx6rLuTzDvCjog75-_qsub1sLYwX_b-G=
eUh2RwqyECoCy8mJ5gdioPpFWqSMDovgX1bqxge1ha9zJIMFKjFmlbk8KfJGdpS6g/4uq/jUICq=
9qARSGfk2tRSsZkkw/h31/h001.DlQKNdNtEW44qUrOlSJ6vGPhL0kDQAIi2aEjtwkGHzE" sty=
le=3D"color: #0077B6;">Reuters/Ipsos survey</a> from late September show th=
ats only a third of Americans approve of strikes on Iran, while approval fo=
r Trump among Republicans had fallen from 82% to 73% in a week.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Polling averages now show Democrats leadin=
g Republicans by roughly nine points on the generic congressional ballot, a=
ccording to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.A=
n7GLjM_3ouXbD4i9O9bXeutqbIhhHdUPvorNE-qy-fLOYkgB_rp1Mjpogu0UcwVUH54k4OY2KH9=
i095Sp9FqKwbrxpp5hI3aCfMvgcN9yF6r6p_gooqvavE9wDDrRwn_auDiZa1b07ItWGGsi1UN4_=
l58gaVBKRwrB1Lrhp6CrUhTSyOJFWLP-LxW-CQ68xZMKt-ElwqOxdhFAE_CrPAyo_0iiCqUMoPs=
II8xOcdDU8ULA7-JL9qnXsDitlYkklWWm_Na3LBIyMGJx4UolvpBf7UpOtQb932XqB1QOswjM/4=
uq/jUICq9qARSGfk2tRSsZkkw/h32/h001.GqhI_fiGoWoGaXrblxyHPm4MsropA_TPca2c5uAj=
95Y" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">forecaster Nate Silver</a>, the widest margi=
n of this election cycle.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Oil prices have also eased on news that <s=
trong>China</strong> is set =E2=81=A0to resume fuel exports, after a pause =
in deliveries during the country=E2=80=99s Golden Week holiday. The resumpt=
ion of exports are expected to boost tight global supplies of diesel, gas, =
and jet fuel.</p>
